# A directory no code decides is a hole in the path, kept by the name the code gives it: the file is that name under
# that directory, and the gap shows.
# What the environment holds stands in the term as its hole; it is no place of its own.

route holeenv.run
step run/Path                                               # `root = Path(os.environ["DATA_DIR"])`
line entry > run call
line File({$DATA_DIR}/report.txt) > run own
line run > Screen own
line run/Path > _·root@run/Path value
line _·root@run/Path > run value   # `(root / "report.txt").read_text()`
home _·root@run/Path run

side entry left
side File({$DATA_DIR}/report.txt) left
side Screen right
